# JSON, as the tree-sitter grammar json gives it: what each kind of its nodes is in the file's tree. A recipe for a
# JSON file says "format json" and then only what its source's parts are.
#   an object and an array hold nodes; a member names what its value is
#   a string is text, its quotes off and JSON's escapes resolved; a number, true and false are text as written
#   null says nothing
grammar json
resolve json
node object group
node array group list
node pair member name key value value
node string text
node number text raw
node true text raw
node false text raw
node null skip
